            <ArticleTitle>Inverted left atrial appendage masquerading as a left atrial mass.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>248-249</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4103/aca.ACA_192_16</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An inverted left atrial appendage after cardiac surgery is a rare finding and can be misinterpreted as a thrombus, mass, or vegetation. We report a case where intraoperative transesophageal echocardiography assisted in making an accurate diagnosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
